---
layout: pattern-library.njk
title: Components
---

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Back button</h2>
  <div class="pl-row">
    <a href="#" class="back-button" aria-label="Back"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i></a>
    <p class="pl-label">.back-button — circular icon-only link, used to return from a detail screen</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Hero panel + drawer</h2>
  <p>.recipe-hero / .recipe-drawer — full-bleed neutral panel topped by a white rounded
    drawer, with a circular image straddling the seam between them. Used on the recipe detail
    screen to hold the dish photo and back button above everything else.</p>
  <div class="recipe-hero">
    <div class="recipe-hero__panel"></div>
    <a href="#" class="back-button back-button--floating" aria-label="Back"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i></a>
    <div class="recipe-hero__image-wrap">
      <img src="/assets/images/bifteki-mit-hirtenkase.jpg" alt="" class="recipe-hero__image">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="recipe-drawer">
    <header>
      <h1>Bifteki auf Orzotto</h1>
      <span class="difficulty">Mittel</span>
    </header>
    <section id="ingredients-section">
      <h2>Ingredients</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>250 g Hackfleisch gemischt</li>
        <li>100 g Hirtenkäse</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Plan hero</h2>
  <p>.planner-hero / .planner-header / .recipe-row — the full-bleed white panel at the top of the
    planner. Holds the eyebrow, heading, and the horizontally scrolling row of circular recipe
    photos for what's currently in the plan. A plain tap opens the recipe preview; holding down
    any item reveals the "×" remove button on all of them at once
    (.recipe-row--removable on the list), shown here for documentation.</p>
  <div class="planner-hero" style="width: auto; margin-inline: 0; margin-top: 0; border: 1px solid #c8c6c2; border-radius: 0.5rem;">
    <div class="planner-header">
      <span class="planner-eyebrow">Your Plan</span>
      <h1>This Week's Recipes</h1>
    </div>
    <ul class="recipe-row recipe-row--removable" style="list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0.5rem 0.25rem;">
      <li class="recipe-row__item">
        <img class="recipe-row__image" src="/assets/images/bifteki-mit-hirtenkase.jpg" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="recipe-row__remove" aria-label="Remove"><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i></button>
        <span class="recipe-row__name">Citrus Bowl</span>
      </li>
      <li class="recipe-row__item">
        <div class="recipe-row__image recipe-row__image--placeholder"><i class="fa-solid fa-utensils"></i></div>
        <button type="button" class="recipe-row__remove" aria-label="Remove"><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i></button>
        <span class="recipe-row__name">Pesto Linguine</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Plan drawer</h2>
  <p>.planner-drawer / .drawer-handle / .planner-menu-wrap--drawer — a full-bleed white
    rounded-top card, the same visual weight as .recipe-drawer above but not seamed to a hero
    image — a centered drag-handle bar marks its top edge instead. The kebab menu floats at the
    drawer's top-right, since "Clear planner" applies to the whole plan, not just the suggestions
    below it. Per-recipe actions like Bring export live in the recipe preview (tapped from a plan
    or suggestion item) rather than in the drawer itself.</p>
  <div class="planner-drawer" style="position: relative; width: auto; margin-inline: 0;">
    <div class="drawer-handle" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="planner-menu-wrap planner-menu-wrap--drawer" style="position: absolute;">
      <button type="button" class="icon-button" aria-label="More options"><i class="fa-solid fa-ellipsis-vertical"></i></button>
    </div>

    <section class="suggestions">
      <h2>Mit ähnlichen Zutaten</h2>
      <p class="suggestions__hint">Rezepte mit denselben Grundzutaten, damit beim Einkauf nichts übrig bleibt.</p>
      <ul class="suggestion-list">
        <li class="suggestion-list__item">
          <img class="suggestion-list__image" src="/assets/images/bifteki-mit-hirtenkase.jpg" alt="">
          <a class="suggestion-list__text" href="#">
            <span class="suggestion-list__name">Tortilla de Patatas</span>
            <span class="suggestion-list__shared">Auch mit: Kartoffeln, Zwiebeln, Eier</span>
          </a>
          <button type="button" class="icon-button icon-button--brand" aria-label="Add to planner"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-plus"></i></button>
        </li>
        <li class="suggestion-list__item">
          <div class="suggestion-list__image suggestion-list__image--placeholder"><i class="fa-solid fa-utensils"></i></div>
          <a class="suggestion-list__text" href="#">
            <span class="suggestion-list__name">Rote-Bete-Carpaccio</span>
            <span class="suggestion-list__shared">Auch mit: Feta</span>
          </a>
          <button type="button" class="icon-button icon-button--brand" aria-label="Add to planner"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-plus"></i></button>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Suggestions</h2>
  <p>.suggestions / .suggestion-list — the planner's primary content: unplanned recipes that
    share base ingredients with the plan, ranked by how many they share. Each card: round
    thumbnail, name, the shared ingredients as a subtle caption, and a solid-brand calendar-plus
    icon-button that adds the recipe to the plan.</p>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Planner menu</h2>
  <p>.planner-menu / .planner-menu__item — a small dropdown card toggled by the drawer's kebab
    button, holding the planner's secondary actions. The destructive action gets the
    .planner-menu__item--danger variant.</p>
  <div class="planner-menu-wrap" style="display: inline-block;">
    <div class="planner-menu" style="position: static;">
      <button type="button" class="planner-menu__item planner-menu__item--danger"><i class="fa-solid fa-trash"></i> Clear planner</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Recipe preview</h2>
  <p>.recipe-preview — bottom-sheet modal shown when a recipe is tapped, as an intermediate step
    before the full detail screen. Used both from the recipe list and from the planner (plan row
    and suggestion cards). Circular image straddles the panel's top edge; the primary action
    navigates to the detail page, the calendar icon-button adds straight to the planner without
    leaving the list. The basket icon-button is optional — only shown when the caller (currently
    just the planner, for already-planned recipes) supplies a Bring export link.</p>
  <div style="position: relative; height: 520px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 1rem; overflow: hidden;">
    <div class="recipe-preview" style="position: absolute; inset: 0;">
      <div class="recipe-preview__backdrop" style="position: absolute; opacity: 1;"></div>
      <div class="recipe-preview__panel" style="position: absolute; bottom: 0; transform: none;">
        <button type="button" class="icon-button recipe-preview__close" aria-label="Close preview">
          <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i>
        </button>
        <div class="recipe-preview__image-wrap">
          <img class="recipe-preview__image" src="/assets/images/bifteki-mit-hirtenkase.jpg" alt="">
        </div>
        <h2 class="recipe-preview__title">Bifteki auf Orzotto</h2>
        <p class="recipe-preview__description">Griechisch inspirierte Frikadellen aus Hackfleisch und Hirtenkäse auf einem cremigen One-Pot-Orzotto.</p>
        <div class="recipe-preview__actions">
          <a class="recipe-preview__cta" href="#">View Full Recipe <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i></a>
          <a class="icon-button" href="#" aria-label="Export to Bring"><i class="fa-solid fa-basket-shopping"></i></a>
          <button type="button" class="icon-button" aria-label="Add to planner"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-plus"></i></button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pl-section">
  <h2 class="pl-section-title">Cook mode</h2>
  <p>.cook-mode — full-screen step-by-step overlay opened from the recipe detail screen's
    "Start cook mode" button, which replaces the old standalone "keep screen on" toggle —
    cook mode now owns the wake lock itself. Shows one step (with its per-step ingredient
    chips, already rendered by the page) at a time in large type spanning the full width,
    readable at a glance while actively cooking. The prev/next controls sit in their own bar
    below the text rather than flanking it, so the text isn't squeezed. Advances via those
    buttons, a left/right swipe on the step, or the arrow keys. Opening it enables the screen
    wake lock; closing it releases it again.</p>
  <div style="position: relative; height: 420px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border-radius: 1rem; overflow: hidden;">
    <div class="cook-mode is-open" style="position: absolute; inset: 0;">
      <div class="cook-mode__header">
        <span class="cook-mode__progress">Step 2 / 6</span>
        <button type="button" class="icon-button" aria-label="Exit cook mode"><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i></button>
      </div>
      <div class="cook-mode__step">
        <div class="step-ingredients">
          <span class="step-ingredients__item"><span class="step-ingredients__qty">400 g</span> Tomaten</span>
        </div>
        Tomaten hinzufügen und 10 Minuten köcheln lassen, bis eine dicke Sauce entsteht.
      </div>
      <div class="cook-mode__controls">
        <button type="button" class="cook-mode__nav cook-mode__nav--prev" aria-label="Previous step"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left"></i></button>
        <button type="button" class="cook-mode__nav cook-mode__nav--next" aria-label="Next step"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right"></i></button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
